        "original_id": "21f4973c-713e-56de-9ff4-d4f9bd7e0031",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Walt Disney Feature Animation, Walt Disney Pictures\n- Films: The Little Mermaid, The Strongest Man in the World, Aladdin, Pocahontas, Dinosaur, Home on the Range, The Prince and the Pauper\n- People: H. Lee Peterson, Kurt Russell, Mickey Mouse\n- Places: Medfield College\n\nFacts:\n- The Strongest Man in the World is a 1975 Disney film starring Kurt Russell as a student at the fictional Medfield College.\n- The Little Mermaid is a 1989 American animated musical fantasy film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation and released by Walt Disney Pictures.\n- H. Lee Peterson was an assistant editor for The Little Mermaid for Walt Disney Pictures.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for Aladdin, Pocahontas, Dinosaur, and Home on the Range for Walt Disney Pictures.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for the short film The Prince and the Pauper, which starred Mickey Mouse, for Walt Disney Pictures.",
